      "note": "The vulnerable sizing loop still iterates every plane after `av1_loop_restoration_filter_frame_init()` skipped disabled ones, reads `ctxt[plane].tile_rect`, and hardcodes the sequence superblock size instead of each active plane's parsed `restoration_unit_size`. That can make `num_rows_lr` smaller than the actual active-plane row count later used by `enqueue_lr_jobs()`, under-sizing both `cur_sb_col` and `job_queue`. The patch fixes both obligations here.",
